            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the case concerns whether the good faith exception to the exclusionary rule should apply when reliance is on precedent that may be altered retroactively."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1812768977ea14d58bdea56b6e4475e435d508ad1553b04fd718b06bc8f902d1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1812768977ea-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner argues that the good faith exception, as labeled, has the same substance and effect as a retroactivity decision."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Michael R. Dreeben (respondent counsel)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1812768977ea14d58bdea56b6e4475e435d508ad1553b04fd718b06bc8f902d1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1812768977ea-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Michael R. Dreeben (respondent counsel), according to Michael R. Dreeben (respondent counsel), the United States contends that the exclusionary rule should be limited to situations necessary to deter police misconduct and shape police conduct."
      }
    ],
